<title>SINGAPORE: DBS in $100 mln issue for Philippine bank.</title>
<headline>DBS in $100 mln issue for Philippine bank.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>DBS Bank said on Monday it has been mandated by the Philippine National Bank (PNB) to arrange a $100 million floating rate certificates of deposit (FRCD) issue.</p>
<p>This is the second FRCD issue that DBS fully underwrote and successfully syndicated this year, said a DBS statement.</p>
<p>The issue is for three years and has a margin of 70 basis points over the three-month London interbank offered rate (LIBOR).</p>
<p>DBS said the issue has received good response from investors and the funds raised will be used by PNB for general funding requirements.</p>
<p>- Singapore Newsroom 65-8703080</p>
